    "kgmemory": {
      "args": [
        "run",
        "-i",
        "-v",
        "claude-memory:/app/dist",
        "--rm",
        "mcp/memory"
      ],
      "autoApprove": [
        "create_entities",
        "create_relations",
        "add_observations",
        "delete_entities",
        "delete_observations",
        "delete_relations",
        "read_graph",
        "search_nodes",
        "open_nodes"
      ],
      "command": "docker",
      "custom_instructions": {
        "text": "This server is a Knowledge Graph Memory store: a persistent, structured, GLOBAL memory shared across every session and working directory (backed by a host-wide Docker named volume, not tied to any project or CWD).\n\nData model: **entities** (a `name`, an `entityType`, and a list of freeform string `observations`), **relations** (directed edges `from` -> `to` with a `relationType`, phrased in active voice), and the observations attached to entities. Together they form a queryable, traversable graph.\n\nGood for: durable, structured facts worth recalling across sessions and projects — people, systems, projects, conventions, decisions, and the relationships between them; anything you want to look up by name or reach by traversing a relation. Keep observations atomic (one fact each) so they can be added and pruned independently.\n\nPoor fit: long freeform prose or narrative notes; transient scratch state; large blobs (logs, file contents, diffs). Store those elsewhere and, if useful, record a short entity/observation here that points to where they live."
      },
      "disabled": false
    }
  },
